## Appendix — process output

## Techniques not applied

- fishbone — not applicable — the assumption space here was narrow enough (cost, funnel, cannibalization, parity) to challenge directly in Phase 2 without a breadth-first category brainstorm; inversion was used instead to surface failure-guaranteeing preconditions.
- theoretical-limit — not applicable — this is a GTM/pricing decision with no governing physical or mathematical hard constraint to strip conventions back to; the relevant ceiling (breakeven conversion rate, chain C2) is a modeled business constraint, not a law-permitted limit.
